  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ on a circle. For each valid iii, AiA_iAi​ and Ai+1A_{i+1}Ai+1​ are adjacent; A1A_1A1​ and ANA_NAN​ are also adjacent.\n\nChef has a sequence of integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​, which he may use to perform any number of operations (including zero). In one operation, he should do the following:\n\n\nChoose an integer iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N).\nChoose iii consecutive integers on the circle.\nChoose a sign S=±1S = \\pm 1S=±1 and add S⋅BiS \\cdot B_iS⋅Bi​ to each of the chosen integers. In other words, either add BiB_iBi​ to each of them or subtract BiB_iBi​ from each of them.\nThe goal is to make all the integers on the circle equal to 000. Can Chef achieve it using these operations?",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤1031 \\le N \\le 10^31≤N≤103",
      "0≤Ai,Bi≤1040 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10^40≤Ai​,Bi​≤104 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10410^4104",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (40 points):** A1=A2=…=ANA_1 = A_2 = \\ldots = A_NA1​=A2​=…=AN​"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing the string `\"YES\"` if it is possible to make all integers on the circle equal to 000 or `\"NO\"` if it is impossible.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5\n1 1 3 3 2\n0 0 2 1 0\n4\n1 1 1 1\n2 2 2 2\n3\n2 0 1\n0 3 5",
        "output": "YES\nNO\nNO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: We can make everything 000 using two operations: choose i=4i = 4i=4 and change the circular sequence (1,1,3,3,2)(1, 1, 3, 3, 2)(1,1,3,3,2) to (1−1,1−1,3−1,3−1,2)=(0,0,2,2,2)(1-1, 1-1, 3-1, 3-1, 2) = (0, 0, 2, 2, 2)(1−1,1−1,3−1,3−1,2)=(0,0,2,2,2), then choose i=3i = 3i=3 and change it to (0,0,2−2,2−2,2−2)=(0,0,0,0,0)(0, 0, 2-2, 2-2, 2-2) = (0, 0, 0, 0, 0)(0,0,2−2,2−2,2−2)=(0,0,0,0,0).\nExample case 2: The parities of integers on the circle cannot change, so they cannot become 000."
      }
    ]
